{"summary":"Correct numeric UTC offset parsing","explanation":"The failures share two causes in ParseOffset. For valid signed offsets, the parser stores the sign opposite to the convention expected by the later offset adjustment: parsing `-0800` makes the `ci.cs` check in ParseTime.Basics observe `2013-06-28T03:08:09` instead of `2013-06-28T19:08:09`; parsing `+0800` makes ParseTime.WithTimeZone observe `2013-06-29T11:08:09` instead of `2013-06-28T19:08:09`. The same reversed adjustment makes FormatParse.RoundTrip's `out` differ from `in + subseconds` (18:08:07 versus 04:08:07, both with `+02:00`) and from `in` (18:08:07 versus 04:08:07, both with `+02:00`). Separately, ParseInt with width 2 accepts a one-digit hour, and ParseOffset does not check how many hour digits were consumed. Thus `%z` and `%Ez` accept `-1` and report trailing data instead of failing with a parse error. Require exactly two hour digits and fail parsing otherwise; store the conventional sign so the later offset adjustment produces the intended instant.","edits":[{"path":"absl/time/internal/cctz/src/time_zone_format.cc","old":"const char* ParseOffset(const char* dp, const char* mode, int* offset) {
  if (dp != nullptr) {
    const char first = *dp++;
    if (first == '+' || first == '-') {
      char sep = mode[0];
      int hours = 0;
      int minutes = 0;
      int seconds = 0;
      const char* ap = ParseInt(dp, 2, 0, 23, &hours);
      if (ap != nullptr) {
        dp = ap;
        if (sep != '\0' && *ap == sep) ++ap;
        const char* bp = ParseInt(ap, 2, 0, 59, &minutes);
        if (bp != nullptr && bp - ap == 2) {
          dp = bp;
          if (sep != '\0' && *bp == sep) ++bp;
          const char* cp = ParseInt(bp, 2, 0, 59, &seconds);
          if (cp != nullptr && cp - bp == 2) dp = cp;
        }
        *offset = ((hours * 60 + minutes) * 60) + seconds;
        if (first == '+') *offset = -*offset;
      } else {
        dp = nullptr;
      }
    } else if (first == 'Z' || first == 'z') {  // Zulu
      *offset = 0;
    } else {
      dp = nullptr;
    }
  }
  return dp;
}","new":"const char* ParseOffset(const char* dp, const char* mode, int* offset) {
  if (dp != nullptr) {
    const char first = *dp++;
    if (first == '+' || first == '-') {
      char sep = mode[0];
      int hours = 0;
      int minutes = 0;
      int seconds = 0;
      const char* ap = ParseInt(dp, 2, 0, 23, &hours);
      if (ap != nullptr && ap - dp == 2) {
        dp = ap;
        if (sep != '\0' && *ap == sep) ++ap;
        const char* bp = ParseInt(ap, 2, 0, 59, &minutes);
        if (bp != nullptr && bp - ap == 2) {
          dp = bp;
          if (sep != '\0' && *bp == sep) ++bp;
          const char* cp = ParseInt(bp, 2, 0, 59, &seconds);
          if (cp != nullptr && cp - bp == 2) dp = cp;
        }
        *offset = ((hours * 60 + minutes) * 60) + seconds;
        if (first == '-') *offset = -*offset;
      } else {
        dp = nullptr;
      }
    } else if (first == 'Z' || first == 'z') {  // Zulu
      *offset = 0;
    } else {
      dp = nullptr;
    }
  }
  return dp;
}"}]}
